              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Impact of Social Media On Cognitive Development of Children And Young Adults: A Systematic Review "
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_unpaywall_primary_10_1186_s12887_025_06041_5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_unpaywall_primary_10_1186_s12887_025_06041_5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This systematic review evaluates the impact of social media usage on cognitive development in children and young adults, focusing on key domains such as attention, memory, executive function, and language development."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulleted-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Gone But Not Forgotten: Investigating The Cognitive Effects of Social Media Content Ephemerality And The Moderating Role of Viewer Involvement"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_informaworld_taylorfrancis_310_1080_10641734_2025_2568874",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_informaworld_taylorfrancis_310_1080_10641734_2025_2568874"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This study examines how content ephemerality affects memory outcomes through two experiments, with a focus on the moderating role of viewer involvement. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulleted-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Consideration of Developmental Stage And The Debate On The Effects of Screens Use - Not All Things Are Created Equal "
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_pubmed_primary_37747728",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_pubmed_primary_37747728"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This article discusses the role of childhood developmental stage in research evaluating the effects of screen use among youth and its application to practice"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bulleted-list",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "list-item",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Can Smartphone Presence Affect Cognitive Function? The Moderating Role of Fear of Missing Out "
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_crossref_citationtrail_10_1016_j_chb_2022_107399",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "https://multisearch.mq.edu.au/permalink/61MACQUARIE_INST/1gnm2jp/cdi_crossref_citationtrail_10_1016_j_chb_2022_107399"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This study examines the influence of smartphones on cognitive function and the potential moderating role of fear of missing out (FOMO). One hundred undergraduate students were randomly recruited and divided into smartphone presence and absence groups to compare the working memory capacity, which is a key element of cognitive function, and the FOMO was also assessed.  "
        }
      ]
